const rewrittenArticles = [
  {label:'Article 01 · LitBuy spreadsheet',title:'LitBuy Spreadsheet: A Practical Way to Compare Finds Before You Order',description:'A new, research-led guide to building a useful shortlist from LitBuy spreadsheet searches.',keywords:'Primary keyword: litbuy spreadsheet · Related: LitBuy finds, Weidian links, Taobao agent, 1688 agent',content:`A LitBuy spreadsheet is most useful when it solves a simple problem: turning hundreds of loosely described marketplace listings into a shortlist you can actually verify. Start by searching for a product type, a visible product ID, or a distinctive phrase from the listing. Do not treat a spreadsheet row as a product promise. Titles, photos, price ranges and stock can all change on the live source listing. Its value is speed: it helps you record what caught your attention, compare similar options, and return to a specific source without relying on memory.

