  {label:'Article 02 · LitBuy QC photos',title:'LitBuy QC Photos: How to Read Warehouse Images Carefully',description:'A new guide to distinguishing visible warehouse evidence from claims a photo cannot support.',keywords:'Primary keyword: LitBuy QC photos · Related: LitBuy inspection, warehouse photos, QC guide',content:`Searchers looking for LitBuy QC photos usually want to know whether warehouse images can answer the question that mattered when they bought an item. LitBuy’s public materials describe a basic quality check and inspection photos for items that arrive at its warehouse. The useful interpretation is narrow: images can document visible details of an item at a particular stage. They can help you compare the colour, quantity, label, obvious shape or included part against your selected option. They cannot prove authenticity, long-term durability, fit, hidden defects, customs acceptance or a future delivery outcome.

