Keep catalogue images and order-specific images separate. A source photo is useful before purchase because it helps form a question. A warehouse image is useful later because it relates to an item that reached that stage. Neither type of image is a guarantee of a wider result. Missing angles are simply missing evidence. Perspective and lighting can make colour and proportion hard to judge. When a photo does not answer a relevant question, do not fill the gap with a guess.

