  {label:'Article 05 · Price guide',title:'LitBuy Price Guide: Read CNY Listings and USD Browsing Prices Correctly',description:'A new article about comparing listings without confusing an estimate with a final payable total.',keywords:'Primary keyword: LitBuy price · Related: LitBuy USD price, CNY conversion, agent cost',content:`The most useful price comparison starts with the source currency. A marketplace listing’s CNY amount is the reference attached to the source item; a USD display makes browsing easier but should be read as an estimate rather than a final quote. Exchange rates move, options vary and the final order can include items that a listing card cannot settle. Keep the original CNY amount next to the USD estimate so you can understand both the source record and the browsing comparison.

