  {label:'Article 09 · Tracking guide',title:'LitBuy Tracking: Read a Parcel Status Without Inventing a Delivery Date',description:'A new tracking guide for turning status updates into useful next actions.',keywords:'Primary keyword: LitBuy tracking · Related: package tracking, parcel status, shipping update',content:`Tracking works best when you preserve the right identifiers from the start. Keep the order ID, parcel ID, tracking number, destination and date of submission together. They are not interchangeable. An order identifies a purchase request; a parcel identifies a group prepared for shipment; a tracking number follows a carrier process. A written record stops several shipments from being mixed together when an update arrives later.

