The purpose of an after-sales checklist is to preserve options, not create false certainty. Keep product and order identifiers, write the question clearly, review the policy that applies now, and separate the product issue from any later carrier or customs issue. That gives you a better factual record and makes it easier to use the correct official channel for the correct stage.`}
